Kelpto includes material from the following sources.

==============================================================================
CommonMark spec
==============================================================================

Kelpto's tests include examples extracted from the CommonMark spec
(https://github.com/commonmark/commonmark-spec), spec.txt at tag 0.31.2:
each example's Markdown and expected HTML, with the name of its section.
They are in tests/commonmark/spec.json and tests/commonmark/examples.temper.md,
a test-only library kept apart from Kelpto's own code, which nothing
imports and which isn't published. scripts/commonmark_spec.py extracts
them the way the spec's own test tools (test/spec_tests.py) read them.

spec.txt is:

    Copyright (C) 2014-16 John MacFarlane

    Released under the Creative Commons CC-BY-SA 4.0 license:
    <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/>.

so the extracted examples, adapted from it, are also under CC-BY-SA 4.0,
not under Kelpto's Apache-2.0 OR MIT license.

